| 34 | RIGHT AFTER, re-ranked by the operator (2026-11-17: the re-order approved; long work lanes wait until every branch settles back into `main` or `develop`) | ONE FACE, in the order the switch reader set (2026-11-14): `C1`'s adapter as its step one (rank 6), then `K20`, then `K21` with `U6`, then `U5` (sealed-store step 3), then `C13` per-face writer islands (a face island per lent face), then `U4` (`F6` slice four) with `B8` wiring the browser's built `switchFace`, then the daemon mount retires and the vessel seat (the faceless half) wears no face (the direction and the islands at lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/project/place-and-face-islands); beside them `K15` steps 4 and 5, `K12`, `U2`, `U3`, `F1`, `F2`, `W4`, `B2`, `F10`, `F12`, `P13`, `S7`, sealed-store step 5, the face-key roll, the control-plane leap (`bags/daemon` into the vessel's control home). Holder: Lares-Awakens (backlog-awakens Wave 6, a band and not one lane): `K20`, `K21` with `U6`, and `U5` run beside rank 4h's floor format turn, `C13`'s node islands start after rank 4h's flip since both reach `open-node-vessel.ts`, then the door and CLI face routing, the ring's narrowing, the mount's retirement; `C1`'s adapter (rank 6) stays in neither backlog yet | A session wears the face and the vessel seat wears none only once the daemon mount retires, and the lent set (`L47h`) bounds the faces that retirement hands to sessions; the band still lands before the second operator seats a key (ranks 35 and 39), as the fence asks, so its rank holds. |

